            <ArticleTitle>Neglected Tropical Diseases, Neglected Communities, and Conflict: How Do We Leave No One Behind?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1471-4922(17)30269-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pt.2017.10.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most well established neglected tropical disease (NTD) programs have seen great progress towards disease control or elimination. Areas in conflict, however, are a looming challenge to reaching control and elimination targets. To be successful, programs and partners need to creatively adapt to local circumstances and embrace new colleagues not traditionally seen as NTD implementers.</AbstractText>
